    "question": "Rory has 30 more jellybeans than her sister Gigi who has 15 jellybeans.  Lorelai has already eaten three times the number of jellybeans that both girls have.  How many jellybeans has Lorelai eaten?",
    "gold": "180",
    "answer": "Rory has 30 more jellybeans than Gigi who has 15 so Rory has 30+15 = <<30+15=45>>45 jellybeans\nRory has 45 jellybeans and Gigi has 15 so that's 45+15 = <<45+15=60>>60 jellybeans total\nLorelai has eaten three times the amount of jellybeans that both girls have so she has eaten 3*60 = <<3*60=180>>180 jellybeans\n#### 180"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many jellybeans Lorelai has eaten, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of jellybeans Rory has.\n2. Determine the total number of jellybeans that both Rory and Gigi have together.\n3. Calculate the number of jellybeans Lorelai has eaten, which is three times the total number of jellybeans that Rory and Gigi have.\n\nFirst, we know that Gigi has 15 jellybeans. Rory has 30 more jellybeans than Gigi, so we can calculate the number of jellybeans Rory has as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of jellybeans Rory has} = 15 + 30 = 45\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the total number of jellybeans that both Rory and Gigi have together:\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of jellybeans} = 15 + 45 = 60\n\\]\n\nLorelai has eaten three times the number of jellybeans that both girls have, so we calculate the number of jellybeans Lorelai has eaten as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of jellybeans Lorelai has eaten} = 3 \\times 60 = 180\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of jellybeans Lorelai has eaten is \\boxed{180}.",
